export default "usage: yoink [global-options] [--run <cmd> [cmd-options] ...] <plan>\n\nGlobal options (before first --run):\n  --schema              print the plan JSON Schema\n  --pipefail            exit non-zero if any piped producer fails (default)\n  --no-pipefail         accept failed piped producer when consumer succeeds\n  --max-bytes <n>       limit each command's captured stdout/stderr to n bytes\n\nCommand flags (repeatable, apply to most recent --run):\n  --run <cmd>           add a command to the plan\n  --label <text>        label for the command (optional, default: command-N)\n  --timeout <seconds>   kill the command after N seconds (default: 1)\n  --cwd <path>          working directory (relative to Yoink's CWD)\n  --pipe                send stdout to the next command's stdin\n  --capture             include stdout in the bundle (overrides piped default)\n  --no-capture          suppress stdout (overrides standalone default)\n\nA plan is a JSON file or stdin stream with a \"commands\" array.\nEach command needs \"label\" and \"run\". Optional fields:\n  cwd       working directory (relative to Yoink's CWD)\n  timeout   seconds before the command is killed (default: 1)\n  pipe      send stdout to the next command's stdin\n  capture   include a piped command's stdout in the output bundle\n\nExamples:\n  yoink plan.json\n  cat plan.json | yoink -\n  yoink --pipefail plan.json\n  yoink --no-pipefail plan.json\n  yoink --run \"cat AGENTS.md\" --label \"Instructions\"\n  yoink --run \"rg --files src\" --label \"Source\" --pipe \\\n        --run \"grep test\" --label \"Filter\"\n  yoink --max-bytes 100000 --run \"cat AGENTS.md\" --label \"Instructions\"\n";
